# The kernel is server-side source: its classes, the modules Nino ships and
# what each of them brings - templates (the mail bodies, the maintenance
# page), texts, install unit, panel scripts. Nothing in here is ever requested
# by a browser. What is public of _nino/ - Nino.css, Nino.js and Nino.ui.js -
# lies beside this directory, and a module's stylesheets and scripts are read
# off disk and bundled into public/.cache/ or _admin/.cache/ like everything
# else (see \Nino\Modules\Assets). A .php file would run and show nothing; a
# template or a text file is no php and would be delivered as it stands.
Require all denied

Options -Indexes
